Criteria for Imposition of Administrative Fines (Related to Article 35)
■ Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Prevention of and Countermeasures against School Violence [Annex] <Amended 2024.2.27>
Criteria for Imposition of Administrative Fines (Related to Article 35)
1. General Criteria
In any of the following cases, the superintendent may reduce the administrative fine specified in the individual criteria under section 2 by up to one-half; provided that this shall not apply to an offender in arrears on administrative fines.
(a) The offender falls under any subparagraph of Article 2-2(1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on the Regulation of Violations of Public Order;
(b) The violation is recognized as resulting from minor negligence or error;
(c) A reduction is otherwise considered necessary in view of the severity, motive and consequences of the violation and other relevant circumstances.
